FEAT-08: ODF AES (CBC and GCM) and the manifest digests over the linked OpenSSL.

The ODF package code (package/source/zipapi/ZipFile.cxx) asks the UNO service com.sun.star.xml.crypto.NSSInitializer for exactly
two things: a digest context (the SHA256_1K manifest checksum) and an AES-CBC / AES-GCM cipher context. That service exists only in
the NSS-based xmlsecurity module, which this WebAssembly build does not have (TLS=OPENSSL), so every AES-encrypted ODF failed to read
and every ODF output protection failed to write.

This adds comphelper/source/crypto/OpenSSL{CipherContext,DigestContext,ContextSupplier}.{hxx,cxx}: a line-for-line port of
xmlsecurity/source/xmlsec/nss/{ciphercontext,digestcontext}.cxx and ONSSInitializer::get{Cipher,Digest}Context from NSS PK11 to
OpenSSL EVP, registered under our own implementation name for that service in comphelp.component and in the static constructor map
(solenv/bin/native-code.py). The XNSSInitializer getters fail closed (no NSS profile). See docs/design/odf-aes-openssl.md for the port
table, the five stated deviations (asserts become exceptions; the context is broken after every failure; GCM buffers grow by hand and
are wiped before they are freed; buffers are cleansed; no secret in any message), the caller audit and the randomness finding.
Tested natively under ASan/UBSan: tests/gates/odf_aes_native.

